cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ChainSight: pre-dispatch late-delivery risk and order margin under a leakage-audited feature set"
message: "If you use this software or its leakage analysis, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Tejas
    family-names: Deshmane
    email: tejasdeshmane66@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/Surge77/ChainSightAI"
url: "https://github.com/Surge77/ChainSightAI"
abstract: >-
  ChainSight predicts, for an order that has not yet shipped, the probability of late
  delivery and the expected margin, and combines the two through a cost-sensitive decision
  engine. Its central contribution is methodological rather than architectural: the DataCo
  Smart Supply Chain dataset's late-delivery label is derived from post-dispatch columns,
  and its profit column is a near-duplicate of a feature. ChainSight removes every column
  unavailable at order time and reports, side by side, what the leaked and the honest
  models score. The modelling is restricted to a fixed scikit-learn curriculum, enforced
  by a static import gate.
keywords:
  - supply chain
  - late delivery prediction
  - data leakage
  - cost-sensitive classification
  - scikit-learn
license: MIT
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-28"
